# Default to CRLF in the working tree (all workstations for this repo are Windows).
#
# Note: `eol` only controls what lands on disk at checkout. Git always stores
# text files as LF in the object database, so the committed blobs are unchanged
# by this file -- it just stops the Linux devcontainer and Windows git from
# disagreeing about the working tree.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Keep LF for files consumed by Linux tooling. Nothing here needs it today
# (no shell scripts, and the Dockerfile uses exec-form CMD), but `COPY . .`
# drops the working tree into a Linux image, so these are cheap guards.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
